<BaseLayout title="How LearnNest works | LearnNest" description="How LearnNest works in three simple steps: find a tutor, book a trial lesson, then keep learning with lesson packs. Demo site." path="/how-it-works">
  <h1>How LearnNest works</h1>
  <p class="lede">Learning a language 1-to-1 online is simple. Here is the whole journey, step by step.</p>

  <h2>Step 1 — Find your tutor</h2>
  <p>Go to <a href="/tutors">Find tutors</a> and search by language, price, rating and availability. Each sample profile shows the tutor’s specialities, languages, sample reviews, and when they teach. Take your time — comparing a few tutors is the best way to find a good fit.</p>

  <h2>Step 2 — Book a trial lesson</h2>
  <p>Choose a 25-minute or 50-minute trial. A 25-minute trial costs half the 50-minute price. In the trial you meet your tutor, talk about your goal and level, and try a short lesson together. On this demo, booking only shows a confirmation on the page — nothing is booked and nothing is charged.</p>

  <h2>Step 3 — Keep learning, your way</h2>
  <p>If the tutor feels right, you would choose a lesson pack — for example 4, 8 or 12 lessons per 28 days — and book lessons at times that suit you. Your tutor plans each lesson around your goal, whether that is work, travel, exams or everyday conversation. If a tutor is not right for you, try another one.</p>

  <h2>What happens in a lesson?</h2>
  <p>In a real marketplace, lessons take place in an online classroom with video, a whiteboard and shared materials — no separate video app needed. On this demo site there is no live classroom; the tutor pages and booking form show how it would look.</p>

  <h2>What do I need?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A computer, tablet or phone with a camera and microphone.</li>
    <li>A stable internet connection.</li>
    <li>A quiet place to talk for 25 or 50 minutes.</li>
  </ul>

  <p><a class="btn" href="/tutors">Find my tutor →</a> <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/pricing">See pricing</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
